        "subject": "LU-20076 osp: do not wait out a disconnect nobody answers",
        "message": "LU-20076 osp: do not wait out a disconnect nobody answers\n\nWhen an MDT stops, each OSP sends a DISCONNECT to its OST or\nMDT and the shutdown waits for the reply. If that target was\nstopped first and its node has no service left, as when\nconf-sanity stops the OSTs and then the MDTs, the request is\ndropped on arrival and the MDT waits for its timeout: the\nconnect timeout plus the network latency estimate, about 10\nseconds with at_min=5. conf-sanity and other suites pay this on\nmost MDT unmounts.\n\nIn osp_shutdown(), wait one second for the reply, then abort the\nrequest and ignore its result. The abort ends only the wait for\nthe reply: the request is still sent before the shutdown goes\non, and a peer that receives it disconnects the export however\nlong it takes to reply, so a slow network or a busy peer loses\nonly the result code. A request not yet sent at that point is\nnot aborted, and is waited for as it is today.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity\nTest-Parameters: testlist=replay-single,recovery-small\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ia20a642cfa140677af411bdc6b6d580944062cf5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
